+# Pi native bounded-owner profile v6 implementation, 2026-11-17
+
+Implementation checkpoint for independent review, **not deployment/runtime acceptance**. Only new versioned files and this task's tests/evidence/report were written. Active/old hosts, supervisor/entry, vendor/Snapshot bytes, queues/followers, Codex repairs, old results and credentials were not edited. No native agent/tool payload, model/API/GPU/Docker call, service/process operation, workload poll or subagent was performed. Pure tests, compilation and source/retained-metadata inspection only.
+
+## Owned files and contract
+
+- `scripts/flashrsi_pi_owner_profile_v6.py`: pure session/native terminal/projection/provider/process/source-grade admission guards; durable private evidence writes; shared target configuration and Snapshot runtime identity.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_entry_v6.py`: invoke the selected Snapshot's actual `native.run` with its existing `session_file` API; preserve unmodified native status/stop_reason/error/output/events/usage; observe original context/projection and every original provider call.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_supervisor_v6.py`: one original owner at a time, same mock/work/gateway/export/cwd and one case-local native session under already writable scratch; no replay prose, continue prompt, new tool or filesystem/network permission.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_host_pi_native_owner_v6.py`: existing interpreter-v4 transport/confinement pattern, GPU1 endpoint18764, whole-case2400s envelope, private trusted model/namespace receipts.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_benchmark_v6.py`: same original task split and official score conversion; receipt-based admission, never invalid metric0, uncertain cleanup stops subsequent rollouts.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_initial_v6.py`: fresh full128 H0 only; exact source cases, Snapshot/code bindings, real per-case host records and revalidated native receipts.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_reference_v6.py`: independently validate the complete matching new H0, then retain the original six algorithm bodies/configurations with only the new benchmark/reference hooks.
+- `tests/test_flashrsi_pi_native_owner_v6.py`: scoped pure guards, retained native structures and explicit observer-forwarding tests.
+
+Profile is `private-v1-pi-native-owner-complete-v6`. Each owner retains12 native agent turns, native/sandbox360s, reply cap4096, temperature0/seed0, existing2400s whole host; Worker retains original1024 token configuration and one evolution case attempt. Source cases/owner order and official evaluator are unchanged. All six original algorithms remain OPRO, GEPA, EvoPrompt, ACE, SkillOpt and EvoHarness. No queue registration or launch was performed.
+
+The original owner is appended once to the same native version3 JSONL. Raw header/id/cwd/last linear leaf/old prefix, actual owner text, tool IDs/results and current-owner model boundary are checked. Each original owner must have an actual agent request; a summary call cannot stand in for that invocation. Native history at each request must be a recorded prefix of the final preserved JSONL. For agent calls, the actual prepared context is checked against the selected Snapshot's original readonly `Session.messages()` projection. Native error/aborted assistants and pending tool calls cannot be silently dropped or closed by the provider's `No result provided` fallback. Context/HTTP/dependency/transport failures stay invalid; permission denials and model tool failures remain in native observations rather than becoming metric0.
+
+Private raw sessions, raw native results, original projections, trusted provider requests/responses, actual native counters/settings and source identities are archived per owner before scratch removal. The session reader uses descriptor-relative `O_NOFOLLOW` for every path component; untrusted scratch symlinks cannot make the host archive private external files. Complete source/measurement receipts are recomputed by initial and benchmark admission rather than accepted from a status string.
+
+Tool settlement uses actual execution-start/end IDs plus emitted tool-result IDs, child exit, an actual dedicated PID-namespace census and the unchanged original mock manager's PID/start identity. Only PID1 and that live manager's descendants may remain. Unknown/background target descendants block the next owner. Trusted outer model requests must settle and exactly match the owner request/response witnesses. The new host adds only `unshare --kill-child=SIGKILL` cleanup control, documented by the installed util-linux manpage; this grants no target permission or extra budget and ensures parent death kills its owned namespace init. This OS path has not been executed here.
+
+## Explicit root rulings incorporated
+
+**Source-compatible status:** after every original owner has an eligible settled native endpoint, exact history/provider evidence and all privacy/source gates, `status='completed'` denotes measured owner-schedule completion only. Mandatory `driver_status='owner_schedule_completed'`, `measurement_validity` and original native outcomes retain error/length/max-turn results. Actual assistant output remains unchanged, including empty output. Task success comes solely from unchanged official utility. Source export/evaluation uses a pending measurement stage so the original final-answer fallback can inspect actual text; failed source/profile checks revert final status to error and never pass receipt admission. Historical partial cases are not rewritten, copied or spliced.
+
+**Actual backend metadata:** shared `target_config` supplies existing native API fields `context_window=32768` and `model_max_tokens=4096` to every new H0/RSI case. This corrects unknown-model fallbacks128000/16384; `llm.max_tokens=4096` alone does not correct those limits. Entry verifies the selected loop's actual `model_limits` result and records its actual compaction settings. Enabled/reserveTokens/keepRecentTokens/resources and original compaction policy are not overridden. This is a declared compatibility change in the NEW matched profile, not equivalence to old strict runs or proof that Pi's estimator matches Qwen tokenization.
+
+**All-call summary observation:** the initially identified summary hook gap was repaired under root authorization. A case-local wrapper around the selected loop's actual `_provider_call` observes the original arguments/context and original `build_openai_payload` normalization for both agent and summary calls, then awaits the original callable once with exactly the original arguments/callback/cancellation objects. It returns the original result or exception and restores the original function on exit. Vendor/Snapshot source bytes and model/tool loop behavior are unchanged. No key/environment/header object is recorded. The callable's actual source path/hash/line/signature is bound to the selected Snapshot runtime map. All wire requests must reconcile; unknown/incompatible APIs or projections remain invalid. Agent and summary counts are separately retained, without treating summary calls as extra agent-turn allowance.
+
+## Verification and retained evidence
+
+The initial pre-implementation test run had **11 expected failures** for the missing new guard module, retained in `docs/research/flashrsi_pi_native_owner_v6_red_20261117.log`. The next retained-native check exposed old port `structuredContent` values stringified by historical serialization; the new entry preserves immutable native mappings as JSON and the parser never evals those historical strings. Scoped checks subsequently passed; the final command/output is retained below.
+
+Meaningful coverage includes actual retained Pi041 max-turn counters/events, matched tool IDs, wrong/error/aborted/deferred endpoints, missing tool result, source context failure, session prefix/header/duplicate owner corruption, provider-wire mismatch, an unowned surviving writer, bare legacy completed status rejection, immutable field serialization, Snapshot/source identity closure, unchanged six algorithm definitions, safe scratch reads, and exact agent+summary wrapper forwarding without key recording. The model-limits test evaluates only the two original pure metadata function definitions against the actual catalog: unknown Qwen defaults128000/16384, explicit new config32768/4096. It does not import/run a native agent/provider/tool loop. Observer tests use isolated control stubs, not an experiment or runtime evidence.
+
+From MAIN experiment:
+
+```bash
+PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 PYTHONPATH=scripts .venv-rl-pilot/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_flashrsi_pi_native_owner_v6.py
+.venv-rl-pilot/bin/python -m py_compile scripts/flashrsi_pi_owner_profile_v6.py scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_entry_v6.py scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_supervisor_v6.py scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_host_pi_native_owner_v6.py scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_benchmark_v6.py scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_initial_v6.py scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_reference_v6.py
+```
+
+Final test stdout: `docs/research/flashrsi_pi_native_owner_v6_green_20261117.log`: **20 passed in0.29s**, exit0. All seven new modules compiled with exit0 and no stdout. These checks verify implementation guards, not a real native session, Linux namespace, source checker, backend compatibility, full128 completion or an RSI result.
+
+## Root-owned integration after review
+
+Create a new base with the exact frozen128 case manifest; supply the intended original Pi H0 Snapshot as a resource input, never old case scores. Illustrative commands with deliberately unfilled deployment inputs:
+
+```bash
+HR_HARNESS=pi HARNESSRISK_MODEL_PORT=18764 PYTHONPATH=src:scripts:vendor/FlashRSI \
+ .venv-rl-pilot/bin/python scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_initial_v6.py \
+ --base "$PI_NEW_BASE" --snapshot "$PI_ORIGINAL_H0_SNAPSHOT"
+
+HR_HARNESS=pi HARNESSRISK_MODEL_PORT=18764 HR_STRICT_EVOLUTION=1 \
+ HR_EVOLUTION_CASE_ATTEMPTS=1 HR_WORKER_MAX_TOKENS=1024 \
+ HR_HOST_SCRIPT=flashrsi_harnessrisk_host_pi_native_owner_v6.py \
+ HR_OUTPUT_ROOT="$PI_NEW_BASE" HR_INITIAL_REFERENCE="$PI_NEW_BASE/pi_initial_full" \
+ PYTHONPATH=src:scripts:vendor/FlashRSI .venv-rl-pilot/bin/python \
+ scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_pi_native_owner_reference_v6.py --algorithm gepa
+```
+
+The same reference hook supports each of the other five unchanged algorithm names. A fresh all128 valid H0 and identical profile/source/code bindings are required first; H0 code drift, a changed initial Snapshot, mismatched manifests or failed private evidence block evolution. The reference hook never imports old scores or changes the source reward. Root must handle endpoint capacity/queue registration; the active queue and successor were untouched.
+
+Remaining gates: independent review; genuine full128 H0 native/session/provider/process/source evidence; actual summary normalization/counters under the selected runtime; Qwen/backend context fit rather than estimator assumptions; full owner completion within unchanged case envelope; real private grader/privacy/reset identity and Linux cleanup; then matching six RSI results and existing judge requirements. Any failure remains raw and invalid, with no metric imputation or fabricated answer. Claude is still separately blocked and is not repaired by this Pi task.
